From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:46:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/49] Instruction hooks: config [[hooks]] emits host calls at
 instruction addresses

A hook is declared by address (before/after, optional redirect) in the recompiler
config. The generated function calls g_ps2InstructionHooks[i] when set; a before
hook returning nonzero jumps to its redirect label. Hosts register with
PS2Runtime::registerInstructionHook. With nothing registered the guest code runs
as recompiled, so games can add mid-function behavior without patching generated
text.

